   195→          - status-cascade
   196→        title: Cascade Status Updates
   197→        type: requirement
   198→        tags:
   199→          - dx
   200→          - cli
   201→        description: >-
   202→          When updating a parent item's implementation status, CLI offers to cascade the update to
   203→          nested children. Prevents status drift between parent features and child requirements.
   204→        depends_on: []
   205→        implements: []
   206→        relates_to: []
   207→        tests: []
   208→        created: '2026-01-16T13:52:53.609Z'
   209→        acceptance_criteria:
   210→          - id: ac-1
   211→            given: >-
   212→              A parent item has children and user runs 'kspec item set @parent --implementation
   213→              implemented'
   214→            when: The command completes
   215→            then: 'CLI prompts: ''Update N child items to implemented? [y/n]'''
   216→          - id: ac-2
   217→            given: >-
   218→              A parent item has children, user runs 'kspec item set @parent --implementation
   219→              implemented', and user responds 'y' to the cascade prompt
   220→            when: The cascade is accepted
   221→            then: All child items are updated to 'implemented' and each child update is logged
   222→          - id: ac-3
   223→            given: >-
   224→              A parent item has children, user runs 'kspec item set @parent --implementation
   225→              implemented', and user responds 'n' to the cascade prompt
   226→            when: The cascade is rejected
   227→            then: Child items are NOT updated and retain their original status
   228→          - id: ac-4
   229→            given: >-
   230→              A parent item has children and user runs 'kspec item set @parent --implementation
   231→              implemented --json'
   232→            when: JSON mode is active
   233→            then: No cascade prompt is shown and children are NOT automatically updated
   234→          - id: ac-5
   235→            given: >-
   236→              A parent item has NO children and user runs 'kspec item set @parent --implementation
   237→              implemented'
   238→            when: The update completes
   239→            then: No cascade prompt is shown (since there are no children to cascade to)
   240→        status:
